{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import monitoring_route with context %}
---
{#
  ONE reader through this route: postflight.py's §9.3 API-key check, which asks for
  /api/v1/indexer because it is the path this route admits. monitor-bridge's
  check_prowlarr_indexers (`monitor-bridge/files/checks/service.py`) reads PROWLARR_URL, a
  ClusterIP (`prowlarr.<ns>.svc.cluster.local:9696`), and never touches Traefik — the template
  comment said otherwise until 2026-09-10 (#1683), carried forward through two rewrites without
  being checked. The prefix covers what postflight reads and covers nothing else:
  /api/v1/indexer is not a prefix of any write endpoint.

  extra_client_cidrs admits the cluster nodes' own host processes, which is what postflight is,
  and `include_bridge_ip=false` drops the macro's default grant. That default is
  `k8s_bridge_client_ip` (10.0.0.161, daniel-server's LAN address), left over from when
  monitor-bridge was a Docker container ON daniel-server; it is dead on this route and was
  measured dead on 2026-09-10. A request from a daniel-server shell to
  `prowlarr.local.<domain>/api/v1/indexer` arrived at Traefik as `ClientHost: 10.42.1.0` and got a 302,
  so the route did not match — 10.0.0.161 never reaches it.

  That measurement also bounds the gateway pair. The addresses are cni0 GATEWAYS, not the nodes'
  LAN addresses: host traffic to the ingress VIP SNATs to a cluster-internal address. Which one
  depends on where the traefik POD sits. Traefik is pinned to daniel-box
  (`kubernetes.io/hostname` nodeSelector), so daniel-box's own host traffic stays local and
  arrives as its cni0 gateway `10.42.0.1` — measured the same day, a 401 from prowlarr rather
  than a 302, which is the route matching and prowlarr rejecting the absent X-Api-Key. Traffic
  from daniel-server crosses the VXLAN overlay and arrives as its flannel.1 address `10.42.1.0`,
  NOT as its cni0 gateway `10.42.1.1`. `10.42.1.1/32` is therefore inert while that pin holds.
  Kept rather than dropped because postflight runs on daniel-box only, so nothing depends on it
  either way, and unpinning traefik is what would make the pair matter. Same variable and the
  same reasoning as loki-homelab's read route, whose `DECIDED 2026-08-24` marker verified the
  daniel-box half live first.

  The path prefix, the LAN-only rule and prowlarr's own X-Api-Key are unchanged.
#}
{{ monitoring_route(container_item.name, container_item.hostname, container_item.port, '/api/v1/indexer',
                    extra_client_cidrs=k3s_cni0_gateways, include_bridge_ip=false) }}
